# What NOT to upload to Vercel.
#
# Why this file exists: the Vercel CLI reads only the ROOT .gitignore. The
# Android and Expo build output under apps/ is excluded by *nested* .gitignore
# files it never sees — so a repo git counts at 2,039 files tried to upload
# 19,614 and hit the CLI's 15,000-file cap:
#
#   Error: Invalid request: `files` should NOT have more than 15000 items
#
# `--archive=tgz` also gets past the cap, but it uploads the same junk in one
# blob. Excluding it is the fix; the flag is the symptom.
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded:
#   packages/  — mw-core is a dependency the web app imports
#   docs/      — src/lib/compliance reads docs/compliance/controls.yaml at
#                runtime, so removing docs/ breaks the deployment, not the build
#   seo/, supabase/, scripts/ — small, and cheaper to keep than to be wrong about

# Native surfaces. Nothing in app/ or src/ imports from here; the web build has
# no use for a Gradle tree (11,159 files, the bulk of the overage). Its build
# output is excluded by apps/android/.gitignore and apps/mobile/.gitignore —
# nested files, hence invisible to the CLI, hence the overage.
apps/

# Agent tooling, including worktrees (115k+ files). Listed explicitly rather
# than relying on whatever the CLI excludes by default.
.claude/

# Build output — Vercel builds from source, so shipping ours is pure weight.
.next/
out/

# Test and report artefacts, regenerated on every run.
test-results/
playwright-report/
coverage/
